---
layout: base.njk
description: geosynced is a GEO and AEO consultancy. We help businesses get cited in ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, Claude and Google AI Overviews, and we track our own citations in public.
faq:
  - q: What is generative engine optimization (GEO)?
    a: GEO is the work of making your business easy for AI search engines to find, understand and cite when they answer a question. Where classic SEO aims for a ranking on a results page, GEO aims for a mention inside the answer itself.
  - q: How is GEO different from AEO?
    a: In practice they overlap almost completely. AEO (answer engine optimization) is the older term and also covers featured snippets and voice assistants. GEO focuses on generative AI answers. We do both, and we measure both the same way, by checking which sources the answers cite.
  - q: Do I still need SEO?
    a: Yes. AI search engines mostly pull from pages that are already crawlable, indexed and trusted. GEO builds on good SEO rather than replacing it.
  - q: How do you measure results?
    a: We run a fixed set of real buyer questions through AI search engines on a schedule and record which sources each answer cites. You see when your pages start appearing, for which questions, and in which engines. Our own site is tracked the same way, in public, on the Live proof page.
  - q: How long does it take to see results?
    a: Technical fixes, such as letting AI crawlers in, can show up within days or weeks. Earning citations for competitive questions usually takes longer, because it depends on content and on what other sites say about you. We show you the data as it comes in rather than promising a date.
---
