<section>
  <div class="split">
    <h2>AI answers name a few sources. Everyone else is invisible.</h2>
    <div>
      <p>A search results page shows ten links. An AI answer usually cites three to five, and most readers never look further. If your site isn't one of them, you aren't in the conversation, even if you rank well on Google.</p>
      <p>Getting cited comes down to three things: AI crawlers can read your pages, your pages answer real questions clearly, and other trusted sites back you up. Most businesses have gaps in all three, and almost none are measuring it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

